  s0: Old session and a queued input
  s1: Seed committed#59; gate holds it
  s2: Restart holds the transition and fence
  s3: Clear began: epoch bumped#59; restart holds the transition
  s4: Exact close confirmed#59; retire and settle
  s5: Clear discarded the queue#59; restart holds the transition
  s6: Old execution retired#59; exclusion still held
  s7: Exclusion released#59; reply pending
  s8: Owner turn began a launch
  s9: A cleared seed was queued again
  s10: Seed waits for the owner
  s11: Owner turn installed Pending
  s12: A launch resumed the conversation a clear ended
  s13: Old execution retired#59; a clear overtook the restart
  s14: Create answered#59; first input not submitted
  s15: First input submitted#59; receipt not committed
  s16: The seed ran after a clear began
  s17: Receipt committed#59; source not bound
  s18: One new Ready session#59; inputs await the owner
  s19: One new Ready session#59; inputs settled once
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: Commit the seed original (acceptance)
  s1 --> s2: Terminate takes transition and fence
  s2 --> s3: User clear begins: bump the clear epoch
  s2 --> s4: Close only the captured pane
  s3 --> s5: Clear discards the queue and the launching input
  s3 --> s3: Close only the captured pane or Retire CAS and settle the old turn
  s4 --> s6: Retire CAS and settle the old turn
  s4 --> s4: Accept an input into the owner queue
  s4 --> s3: User clear begins: bump the clear epoch
  s5 --> s2: Clear's teardown acts on the row
  s6 --> s7: Disconnect keeping selector, release, wake
  s6 --> s3: User clear begins: bump the clear epoch
  s7 --> s8: Owner starts the front: register the launch
  s7 --> s10: Reply to the command
  s3 --> s9: Queue the seed again after the clear
  s5 --> s4: Clear's teardown acts on the row
  s8 --> s11: Install Pending over the vacant row
  s9 --> s12: Owner starts the front: register the launch
  s10 --> s8: Owner starts the front: register the launch
  s5 --> s9: Queue the seed again after the clear
  s5 --> s13: Clear's teardown acts on the row
  s4 --> s13: Retire CAS and settle the old turn
  s11 --> s14: Create the pane once
  s12 --> s12: Install Pending over the vacant row or Create the pane once
  s13 --> s9: Queue the seed again after the clear
  s14 --> s15: Submit the first input
  s12 --> s16: Submit the first input
  s15 --> s17: Commit the input's receipt
  s9 --> s9: Reply to the command
  s17 --> s18: Bind the source
  s9 --> s16: Submit the first input
  s18 --> s19: Submit an input to the successor once
  s19 --> s18: Accept an input into the owner queue
  s16 --> s16: Commit the input's receipt or Bind the source
